<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banu Kanz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Banu Kanz were an Arab tribal dynasty of the Aswan region on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s southern frontier, descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabia">Rabi'a</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> who settled there in the 9th century and intermarried with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubians">Nubians</a>. Their leaders bore the title Kanz al-Dawla, granted by the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>. In the early 14th century Kanz al-Dawla, who claimed the throne of Makuria through descent from its royal family, fought for the crown, and the Banu Kanz furthered the spread of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>.</p></div>
